Sval: no Firefox Messaging System targeting snapshot at startup

BrowserGlue's BackgroundUpdate idle task writes targeting.snapshot.json for
the background update task, which reads it to run Nimbus, the Firefox
Messaging System and its telemetry ping. Sval runs none of them. Taking the
snapshot evaluates every ASRouter targeting attribute, and two of those act:
`needsUpdate` makes a foreground update check, and `crashData` lists the
crash-reports folder. No pref turns the snapshot off, so the call goes;
scheduling the background update task itself is left as it is.

diff --git a/browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs b/browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs
index 97dee13c12..70457a35af 100644
--- a/browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs
@@ -1226,14 +1226,6 @@ BrowserGlue.prototype = {
             let { BackgroundUpdate } = ChromeUtils.importESModule(
               "resource://gre/modules/BackgroundUpdate.sys.mjs"
             );
-            try {
-              await BackgroundUpdate.scheduleFirefoxMessagingSystemTargetingSnapshotting();
-            } catch (e) {
-              console.error(
-                "There was an error scheduling Firefox Messaging System targeting snapshotting: ",
-                e
-              );
-            }
             await BackgroundUpdate.maybeScheduleBackgroundUpdateTask();
           }
